title: PT_D1_Start
---
// ================================================================
// PLAYTEST_Demo.yarn — a three-day mini game (three customers a day) that is
// also the play test of every system in the game today, and the reference for
// writing a new day.
//
// Run: the Day Schedule on [GameLoop] › FlowWiring needs rows for days 1-3 with
//      Start Nodes PT_D1_Start / PT_D2_Start / PT_D3_Start, then Play.
//
// What each day tests:
//   Day 1  Isla / Cole / Faye     named order, order by flavour, random order from
//                                 preferences, flow_check_events (no popup on day 1),
//                                 every short-form character command, wait_scene
//   Day 2  Walter / Owen / Claire random order, order by type, story unlock mid-day
//                                 (the Rum bottle appears on the bar at once), long-form
//                                 character commands, Cut_Camera
//   Day 3  Eliana / Arthur / Isla Event popup at day start (Whiskey, Dry Vermouth,
//                                 Peppermint from the table + Rum from day 2's story),
//                                 ingredient_unlocked, end of shift, summary, thank-you
//
// Not used: save_chapter_node ([SaveLoadSystem] is inactive in the main scene and the
// dialogue would hang, Docs/YarnCommands/save_chapter_node.md).
//
// Lines starting with (PT) print what the game state should be; delete them in a real
// day. (Not "[PT]": Yarn reads square brackets as markup and the speaker name breaks.)
//
// The shape of a day (copy this when writing a new one):
//   BeforeOpen › Event   : the day's popups (new ingredients) show before the start node.
//   BeforeOpen › Story   : the day's start node, set in the Day Schedule
//                          (Day / Start Node / Chapter Name). Pre-opening story.
//                          <<flow_check_events>> shows any popups mid-story.
//                          <<flow_open_bar>> ends it (required, or the day hangs here);
//                          it waits until the chapter title has faded out.
//   Open › Talking       : customers walk in, talk, order.
//                          <<flow_prepare_drinks>> + <<wait_for_task>> = the player
//                          makes the drink; the story waits until it is served.
//   Close                : <<flow_close_bar>> from Talking.
//   next day             : <<flow_next_day>> from Close adds 1 to $day. The next
//                          day's start node begins when THIS dialogue ends, so
//                          make flow_next_day the last thing in the day.
//
// Camera and bar lock are the flow's job (the day opens on MainCam, mouse look only
// while picking ingredients, back to MainCam after serving). Writers only use
// Switch_Camera / Cut_Camera to direct a shot. Camera ids: MainCam (the bar),
// Char1Cam / Char2Cam / Char3Cam (one customer), Char12Cam / Char23Cam (two side by
// side), WideCam (everyone), FrontCam / BackCam, SummaryCam.
// Customer numbers (Order_Cocktail_OutName): Cole 1, Owen 2, Walter 3, Faye 4,
// Isla 5, Claire 6, Eliana 7, Arthur 8. Standing spots: 0-3.
// ================================================================

// A new day starts with a clean Event Log.
<<eventlog_clear>>

Player: (PT) Day {$day}. flow_phase = {flow_phase()}, flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect 1 / BeforeOpen / StoryBeforeOpen) #line:058471b 
Player: My first night behind the bar. #line:014673e 
Player: The old owner left me eight bottles and a note: "Learn these first." #line:0eb602b 
Player: (PT) Gin = {ingredient_unlocked("Gin")} (True), Whiskey = {ingredient_unlocked("Whiskey")} (False until day 3) #line:03569c7 

Player: Let me check the notice board before I open. #line:0346e8b 
// Back to Event: shows any queued popups and waits until they are closed and faded out.
// Day 1 has no unlock popup, so it passes at once.
<<flow_check_events>>
Player: (PT) After flow_check_events: flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect StoryBeforeOpen, no popup on day 1) #line:0728a4a 
Player: Nothing on it yet. Right. Lights on. #line:0bdd410 
<<wait_scene 1>>

// Leaves BeforeOpen for Open › Talking. The Chapter Name fades in and out; the next line waits.
<<flow_open_bar>>
Player: (PT) flow_phase = {flow_phase()}, flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect Open / TalkingWithCustomer, chapter title gone) #line:0545c7c 
<<jump PT_D1_Isla>>
===

title: PT_MakeDrink
---
// Shared by every order: <<detour PT_MakeDrink>> comes back to the line after it.
// The player normally makes the drink; the second option walks every step from Yarn
// instead (no ingredients, so it scores Fail) to show the step commands and speed up a run.
Player: (PT) Order: name = "{order_name()}", type = {order_type()}, flavour = "{order_flavor()}" #line:03ddbd1 

// Pre-selects the minigame of step 2.2. The player's Shake/Stir button overrides it.
<<flow_minigame Shaking>>

-> Make the drink #line:0a0bd1a 
    <<flow_prepare_drinks>>
-> (Test) Let Yarn walk the steps #line:05755fb 
    <<flow_prepare_drinks>>
    Player: (PT) step = {flow_step()} (expect AddIngredient) #line:0a3f1a2 
    <<flow_ingredient_added>>
    Player: (PT) flow_ingredient_added: step = {flow_step()}, minigame = {flow_minigame_type()} (expect Minigame / Shaking) #line:000c1d2 
    <<flow_another_ingredient>>
    Player: (PT) flow_another_ingredient: step = {flow_step()} (expect AddIngredient) #line:0896149 
    <<flow_ingredient_added Stirring>>
    <<flow_drink_complete>>
    Player: (PT) flow_drink_complete: step = {flow_step()} (expect Garnish) #line:0fa5585 
    <<flow_remake_drink>>
    Player: (PT) flow_remake_drink: step = {flow_step()} (expect AddIngredient, nothing scored) #line:0ce41be 
    <<flow_ingredient_added>>
    <<flow_drink_complete>>
    <<flow_garnish_done>>
    Player: (PT) flow_garnish_done: step = {flow_step()} (expect Serve) #line:0d443ae 
    <<flow_serve_done>>

// Waits until the drink is served and scored, then writes $satisfaction and
// $type_of_cocktail. After the test option it returns at once.
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
Player: (PT) Served: order_satisfaction = {order_satisfaction()}, type = {$type_of_cocktail}, minigame = "{flow_minigame_result()}" #line:0f21401 
===

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  DAY 1
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

title: PT_D1_Isla
---
// ── Customer 1: a named order ───────────────────────
<<Isla Enter 1>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController Char2Cam>>
<<Isla Happy>>
Isla: [wave]Evening! Is this place open?[/wave] #line:0967425 
Player: Just opened. You're my very first customer. #line:0e51152 
<<Isla Look L>>
Isla: Cosy. Smells like old wood and lemons. #line:056b301 
<<Isla Look R>>
Isla: And that window... you can see the whole square from here. #line:0045629 
<<Isla Neutral>>

// order_customer names who the next order is for (it scores their preferences).
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Isla>>
Isla: I'll have a [order]{Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutName("Gin Fizz")}[/order], please. #line:0341008 
Player: A Gin Fizz. Let me see... {Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutDescription("Gin Fizz")} #line:0d24452 
<<Cut_Camera CamController MainCam>>
<<detour PT_MakeDrink>>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<Isla Happy>>
    Isla: [bounce]Perfect. Exactly how I like it.[/bounce] #line:03ebd5f 
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    Isla: Not bad. A little different, but fine. #line:024a233 
<<else>>
    <<Isla Sad>>
    Isla: [shake]Hmm... that's not what I asked for.[/shake] #line:0ec9c31 
    <<Isla Sad2>>
    Isla: It's fine. Really. #line:07febeb 
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<Isla Neutral>>
Isla: I'll tell my friends about you. #line:062e4ef 
<<Isla Exit>>
<<jump PT_D1_Cole>>
===

title: PT_D1_Cole
---
// ── Customer 2: an order by flavour (description only, no name) ──
<<Cole Enter 2>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController Char23Cam>>
<<Cole Neutral>>
Cole: Long shift at the mill. I don't know drink names. #line:01df98b 
<<Cole Sad>>
Cole: Just... something like this: #line:035bb31 
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Cole>>
Cole: "[order]{Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutDescription("Sea Breeze")}[/order]" #line:04b47d3 
Player: (PT) order_name = "{order_name()}" (the player is not told; the post-it shows the flavour) #line:02d5bb7 
Player: I think I know what you mean. #line:072b3f0 
<<Cut_Camera CamController MainCam>>
<<detour PT_MakeDrink>>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    Cole: Not quite. Thanks anyway. #line:020abc0 
<<else>>
    <<Cole Happy>>
    Cole: [wiggle]That's the one.[/wiggle] #line:043e2ba 
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<Cole 0>>
<<Cole Exit>>
<<jump PT_D1_Faye>>
===

title: PT_D1_Faye
---
// ── Customer 3: a random order from her preferences ──
<<Faye Enter 3>>
<<Faye Happy>>
Faye: Hi! I've heard there's a new bartender. #line:0d8b738 
Player: That's me. What can I get you? #line:00d4337 
<<Faye Neutral>>
Faye: Surprise me. Something I'd like. #line:0a69705 
// The argument is the customer's number. OutName and OutDescription of the same call
// return the same drink. Only drinks the player can make today are picked.
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Faye>>
Player: How about a [order]{Order_Cocktail_OutName(4)}[/order]? #line:0023e25 
Player: {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(4)} #line:074e528 
Faye: Sounds lovely. #line:02bc9e2 
<<detour PT_MakeDrink>>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<Faye Happy>>
    Faye: [bounce]You read my mind![/bounce] #line:038d851 
<<else>>
    <<Faye Sad>>
    Faye: Mm. Maybe next time. #line:0b37d13 
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<Faye Look L>>
Faye: Oh, it's late. Good night! #line:09bdbd2 
<<Faye Exit>>
<<jump PT_D1_Close>>
===

title: PT_D1_Close
---
Player: That's everyone for tonight. #line:0387a4d 
<<flow_close_bar>>
Player: (PT) flow_phase = {flow_phase()} (expect Close) #line:08a956a 
<<Panel_FadeOut Panel_Transition>>
Player: (Wiping the counter in the dark, I count the takings. Not bad for a first night.) #line:0614f4c 
<<Panel_FadeIn Panel_Transition>>
// Close -> BeforeOpen: $day becomes 2. Day 2's start node begins when this dialogue ends.
<<flow_next_day>>
===

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  DAY 2
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

title: PT_D2_Start
---
<<Panel_FadeOut Panel_Transition>>
<<eventlog_clear>>
Player: (PT) Day {$day}. flow_phase = {flow_phase()}, flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect 2 / BeforeOpen / StoryBeforeOpen, no popup: nothing unlocks on day 2) #line:0484ec0 
Player: Second night. Word must be getting around. #line:0f1158c 
<<flow_open_bar>>
<<jump PT_D2_Walter>>
===

title: PT_D2_Walter
---
// ── Customer 1: random order + a story unlock mid-day ──
<<Walter Enter 1>>
<<Walter Neutral>>
Walter: Evening, son. I knew the old owner. #line:0fa06fb 
Walter: He left this with me. Said to give it to whoever took over. #line:0f31f2e 
Player: A bottle of rum? #line:0732f3d 
<<Walter Happy>>
Walter: It's yours now. #line:00f5339 
// Unlocks Rum for good. The bottle appears on the bar at once; the popup about it
// waits for tomorrow's Event.
<<unlock_ingredient Rum>>
Player: (PT) Rum = {ingredient_unlocked("Rum")} (True, the Rum bottle should be on the bar now) #line:0914c14 

<<Walter Neutral>>
Walter: Now, surprise me. Something I'd like. #line:053f0f1 
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Walter>>
Player: How about a [order]{Order_Cocktail_OutName(3)}[/order]? #line:0e05735 
Walter: Go on then. #line:0191bd9 
<<detour PT_MakeDrink>>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<Walter Sad>>
    Walter: [shake]Not my sort of thing.[/shake] #line:0f6ac67 
<<else>>
    <<Walter Happy>>
    Walter: [wiggle]You've got a knack for this.[/wiggle] #line:00fcc58 
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<Walter Neutral>>
Walter: I'll sit a while, if you don't mind. #line:085ee18 
<<jump PT_D2_Owen>>
===

title: PT_D2_Owen
---
// ── Customer 2: an order by type (any drink of that type counts) ──
<<Owen Enter 3>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController Char23Cam>>
<<Owen Happy>>
Owen: [bounce]Hey hey! Walter, you old fox, you found the new place first![/bounce] #line:03de824 
<<Walter Look R>>
Walter: Some of us have taste, Owen. #line:0f1778c 
<<Walter Neutral>>
<<Owen Happy1>>
Owen: Something strong for me. I don't care what. #line:01fe245 
// Instance command: the first word is the GameObject name "[CocktailSystem]".
// order_name() stays empty: any HighAlcohol drink is right.
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Owen>>
<<order_by_type "[CocktailSystem]" HighAlcohol>>
Player: (PT) order_type = {order_type()} (expect HighAlcohol), order_name = "{order_name()}" (expect empty) #line:06b01e8 
Player: One strong drink coming up. #line:00c0e28 
<<Cut_Camera CamController MainCam>>
<<detour PT_MakeDrink>>

<<if $type_of_cocktail == TypeOfCocktail.HighAlcohol>>
    Owen: [bounce]Now THAT's strong![/bounce] #line:07695eb 
<<else>>
    <<Owen Sad>>
    Owen: That's... juice, buddy. #line:08e0de2 
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<Owen Neutral>>
<<Owen Exit>>
<<Walter Exit>>
<<jump PT_D2_Claire>>
===

title: PT_D2_Claire
---
// ── Customer 3: the long-form character commands ──
<<CharacterEnter CharacterName.Claire 2>>
<<CharacterExpression CharacterName.Claire Amaze>>
Claire: Oh! It's actually open! The old place has been dark for months. #line:068b588 
<<CharacterLook CharacterName.Claire L>>
Claire: You kept the old mirror. Good. #line:0b672ca 
<<CharacterLook CharacterName.Claire F>>
<<CharacterExpression CharacterName.Claire Neutral>>
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Claire>>
Claire: A [order]{Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutName("Cosmopolitan")}[/order], and don't skimp on the cranberry. #line:0f58a85 
<<detour PT_MakeDrink>>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<CharacterExpression CharacterName.Claire Happy>>
    Claire: Lovely. I'll be back. #line:0c70077 
<<else>>
    <<CharacterExpression CharacterName.Claire Rage>>
    Claire: [shake]That is NOT a Cosmopolitan.[/shake] #line:04b7cfb 
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<CharacterExit CharacterName.Claire>>
<<jump PT_D2_Close>>
===

title: PT_D2_Close
---
Player: Quieter than I hoped, but they'll be back. #line:0943600 
<<flow_close_bar>>
<<Panel_FadeOut Panel_Transition>>
Player: (Rum on the shelf now. Tomorrow the supplier brings more bottles.) #line:0702c29 
<<Panel_FadeIn Panel_Transition>>
// $day becomes 3: day 3's Event shows the unlock popup before PT_D3_Start.
<<flow_next_day>>
===

